-// Linux platform IO — safe partial-write implementation selected by the
-// `module_variants` entry in `vzed.json`.
-//
-// On Linux, portable output is performed through the POSIX `write(2)` syscall.
-// The native ABI is declared inline via a VZed-managed `unistd.h` header module
-// so the source tree carries no dependency on host libc headers (the compiler
-// owns the declarations; the linker resolves symbols against the target's C
-// library).
-//
-// Safety rules enforced here (.10, "Portable and safe STD I/O"):
-//   * explicit write() ABI signature declared inline in unistd.h;
-//   * UTF-8 byte-length computed on the TypeScript side — never `string.length`;
-//   * partial-write loop: every non-negative return value advances the pointer
-//     and decrements the remaining count until all bytes have been emitted,
-//     or a real error is observed;
-//   * explicit EINTR/error policy: inspect errno after a negative write()
-//     return — if errno == EINTR, retry exactly once; otherwise propagate an
-//     Error describing the failure. A transient signal interruption never
